      "reconciliation": {
        "delivered": "draft",
        "draft": "Nicco's thanks hang in the air, a polite reflex to no one in particular, since no one has spoken to him. Mistress Elara stands nearby in the square, her elegant fan snapping open with a practised flick, stirring the warm afternoon air. The leather boots remain at her hip, undisturbed—she has not offered them, and he has not received them. Her green-hazel eyes catch the movement of his turning, and she tilts her head, platinum-blonde hair shifting like liquid silk.\n\n\"Are you well, sir?\" Her voice carries that warm, theatrical concern of someone who asks strangers after their health a dozen times a day. \"You seem perhaps a little lost in your own thoughts.\" She does not approach closer, maintaining whatever distance polite traffic in Heartstone Square allows, but her attention is fully upon him now—assessing, curious, the fan's painted silk catching light as it moves.",
        "issues": []
      },
